# Styles

Use Tailwind v4 utility classes and shadcn/ui tokens from
`src/app/globals.css`. Do not add a second CSS framework or ad-hoc
global stylesheets.

- Prefer existing `button`, `card`, `dialog`, `input`, `textarea` primitives.
- Style via `className` + `cn()` (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`).
- The app is always dark (Dark Blue academic theme). Semantic tokens map to
  it: `bg-background` = slate-950, `bg-card` = slate-900, borders slate-800,
  `primary` = sky-400. Use `sky-400` for active state and `indigo-500` for
  completed steps and phase gates.
- Keep the three-panel workspace readable: stepper, chat, Project Brain
  share spacing and type scale.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div style={{ color: "#333", fontFamily: "Inter" }} />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="text-foreground font-sans">
  <Card className="border bg-card" />
</div>
```
